.TH SDL_SIZE_MAX 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_SIZE_MAX \- The largest value that a
.BR size_t
can hold for the target platform.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_stdinc.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_SIZE_MAX SIZE_MAX
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION

.BR size_t
is generally the same size as a pointer in modern times, but this can get weird on very old and very esoteric machines\[char46] For example, on a 16-bit Intel 286, you might have a 32-bit \(dqfar\(dq pointer (16-bit segment plus 16-bit offset), but
.BR size_t
is 16 bits, because it can only deal with the offset into an individual segment\[char46]
.PP
In modern times, it\(aqs generally expected to cover an entire linear address space\[char46] But be careful!

.SH AVAILABILITY
This macro is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

